      <p>
        The Mediterranean island nations of <strong>Cyprus</strong> and <strong>Malta</strong> represent the two premier English-speaking common-law jurisdictions in the European Union for international remote founders, technology executives, and digital nomads seeking legal tax residency. Both countries maintain sophisticated, OECD-compliant tax incentives specifically engineered to attract mobile human capital and foreign investment.
      </p>
