        1. Executive Comparison: Cyprus Non-Dom vs Malta Nomad Residence Scheme
      </h2>
      <p>
        To evaluate which jurisdiction best matches your operational setup, one must look beyond headline rates to the interplay between corporate dividend extraction, cross-border banking, and physical presence requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cyprus is predominantly favored by <strong>software bootstrappers, agency owners, and venture-backed founders</strong> who derive the vast majority of their income through company dividends. Because non-domiciled tax residents in Cyprus are 100% exempt from the SDC (which normally levies 17% on dividends), distributions from an offshore entity, US LLC, UK Ltd, or a Cyprus holding company arrive entirely tax-free, save for a modest 2.65% healthcare contribution capped at €4,770 annually.
      </p>
      <p>
        Malta's Nomad Residence Permit is optimized for <strong>high-earning remote employees and contractors</strong> employed by non-EU corporations who desire immediate Schengen residency. Introduced by Residency Malta Agency, the permit offers a straightforward 10% flat tax on authorized gross remote income, bypassing Malta's standard progressive personal income tax brackets (which escalate rapidly up to 35% on earnings above €60,000).
      </p>

