        <li><strong>Corporate Founders (Dividends &gt;€150,000):</strong> Cyprus becomes dramatically superior. Because dividends are 0% SDC and GESY caps at €4,770, an entrepreneur earning €300,000 in dividends pays an aggregate effective tax rate of just <strong>1.59%</strong>. In Malta, remitting those dividends would trigger up to 35% income tax.</li>
        <li><strong>High-Frequency Travelers:</strong> Anyone who travels more than 300 days a year across Asia, Latin America, and North America will find meeting Malta's 183-day presence requirement impossible. Cyprus's 60-day rule is the only EU framework legally compatible with true global nomadism.</li>
      </ul>

